# Commands Reference

This project provides commands via two interfaces: **Make** targets for common
workflows and a **project CLI** for fine-grained control.

## Make commands

`make help` lists every target, grouped by area. Each target documents itself in the
`Makefile` (`## description` on its line), so the list cannot fall out of date; this page
gives only the entry points.

| Command | Use |
|---------|-----|
{%- if enable_docker %}
| `make quickstart` | First run from a fresh clone: configuration, development stack, migrations{% if use_jwt %}, a development administrator{% endif %} |
| `make dev` | Development stack in Docker, source mounted, reload on change |
| `make prod-local` | The production stack on this machine: production images and settings, random local secrets, plain HTTP |
| `make prod` | Production behind Traefik with TLS (secrets in `backend/.env`) |
{%- endif %}
| `make install` | The backend on the host, without Docker |
| `make test`, `make lint` | Tests; lint, format and type checks |
| `make openapi`, `make openapi-check` | Write or check the API contract (`openapi/openapi.json`) |
{%- if use_frontend %}
| `make client` | Regenerate the frontend API client from the contract |
{%- endif %}
| `make docs`, `make docs-serve` | Build or preview the documentation |
| `make skills` | Install the agent skills of the components |

