```

{%- if enable_rag %}

### RAG Commands

All RAG commands are custom commands invoked via `cmd`:

#### Document Ingestion

```bash
# Ingest a single file
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/guide.pdf

# Ingest a directory
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/

# Ingest recursively into a specific collection
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/ --collection knowledge --recursive

# Ingest with sync mode
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/ --sync-mode new_only
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/ --sync-mode update_only

# Skip replacing existing documents
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-ingest ./docs/ --no-replace
```

#### Search

```bash
# Search the default collection
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-search "what is fastapi"

# Search a specific collection
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-search "deployment guide" --collection docs

# Get more results
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-search "deployment" --top-k 10
```

#### Collection Management

```bash
# List all collections with stats
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-collections

# Show overall RAG system statistics
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-stats

# Drop a collection (with confirmation)
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-drop my_collection

# Drop without confirmation
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-drop my_collection --yes
```

{%- if enable_google_drive_ingestion %}

#### Google Drive Sync

```bash
# Sync from Google Drive root
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sync-gdrive --collection docs

# Sync from a specific folder
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sync-gdrive --collection docs --folder-id abc123
```
{%- endif %}

{%- if enable_s3_ingestion %}

#### S3/MinIO Sync

```bash
# Sync from S3 bucket root
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sync-s3 --collection docs

# Sync from a specific prefix (folder)
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sync-s3 --collection docs --prefix documents/

# Sync from a specific bucket
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sync-s3 --collection docs --bucket my-bucket
```
{%- endif %}


#### Sync Source Management

```bash
# List configured sync sources
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-sources

# Add a new sync source
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-source-add \
    --name "My Drive" \
    --type gdrive \
    --collection docs \
    --config '{"folder_id": "abc123"}' \
    --sync-mode new_only \
    --schedule 60

# Remove a sync source
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-source-remove <source-id>
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-source-remove <source-id> --yes  # Skip confirmation

# Trigger sync for a specific source
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-source-sync <source-id>

# Trigger sync for all active sources
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd rag-source-sync --all
```
{%- endif %}

## Adding Custom Commands

Commands are auto-discovered from `app/commands/`. Create a new file:

```python
# app/commands/my_command.py
import click
from app.commands import command, success, error

@command("my-command", help="Description of what this does")
@click.option("--name", "-n", required=True, help="Name parameter")
def my_command(name: str):
    """Your command logic here."""
    success(f"Done: {name}")
```

Run it:

```bash
uv run {{ project_slug }} cmd my-command --name test
```

For more details, see `docs/en/guides/adding_features.md`.
